+## Board publication
+
+A board can be published, which makes it readable for anyone who has its secret
+public URL. The URL is only disclosed to board administrators and can be
+revoked by unpublishing the board again. Only board administrators can publish
+and unpublish a board.
+
+A published board is served without an account prefix, since the key in the URL
+is the credential:
+
+| Page | URL |
+|------|-----|
+| Board | `GET /public/boards/:key` |
+| Column | `GET /public/boards/:key/columns/:column_id` |
+| Card | `GET /public/boards/:key/cards/:card_number` |
+
+Only published cards are visible on a public board, drafts are not.
+
+The board JSON exposes the link of a published board as `public_url`. It is
+`null` as long as the board isn't published.
+
+### `POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Publishes the board. Only board administrators can publish a board.
+
+__Response:__
+
+Returns `201 Created` with the board in the same shape as `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id`,
+including its new `public_url`.
+
+### `DELETE /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Unpublishes the board. Its public URL stops working. Only board administrators
+can unpublish a board.
+
+__Response:__
+
+Returns `204 No Content` on success.
+
 ## Board Accesses
 
 Board accesses let you see who has access to a board and their involvement level (watching or access only). Any board member can view this information.
